# Local testing
- Start test servers with OTP logging and a separate port, so no real SMS is sent (the dev database may have an SMS provider selected):
  ```bash
  cd apps/api && OTP_PROVIDER=log PORT=4100 nohup pnpm exec tsx src/server.ts > ~/.cache/shop-build/api-test.log 2>&1 &
  ```
- Stop every server you started before finishing (`pkill -f "tsx src/server.ts"`, then check with `pgrep`).
- Seed accounts: `admin@shop.test` and `staff@shop.test`, password `shop-dev`. Customer `+919000000002` (OTP in the API log).
- Test orders with the test payment gateway and the `mock` or `manual` carrier. Never create shipments, pickups or labels against a live carrier account while testing: they book real couriers and cost money. Carrier tests use recorded sample responses, never real API calls.
- API tests: `pnpm test` (per-run test database; needs the dev PostgreSQL and Redis). Don't run it alongside a Docker or Next.js build.
- WSL memory is limited: run one heavy build at a time (Next.js build, Docker build) and write logs to `~/.cache/shop-build/`, not `/tmp` (WSL restarts wipe it).

# Deploying and building apps
Follow `docs/deployment.md` (runbook and the table of current clients). The rules that must not be skipped:
- Deploy only what the developer has pushed; the server pulls from GitHub. There are no automatic deploys: CI only checks.
- Before deploying, check the deployed commit and read every pending migration (`git diff --name-only <deployed>..origin/main -- apps/api/prisma/migrations`). If one moves data, drops columns or adds `NOT NULL`, check it against the live data and run an on-demand backup first.
- After deploying, confirm `docker compose ps` is healthy and `/health` is `ok`.
- Update every client's server before handing out new app builds.
- Each client is isolated: never reuse secrets, EAS projects, Firebase projects or carrier and payment accounts between clients, and never point one client's app or website at another's API.
- App builds: per-client values go in that client's `eas.json` profiles and `brands/<brand>/`. `APP_ID` is permanent once published; never change it for a published app. Never delete EAS credentials (signing keys). Submit with `--id <build id>`, never `--latest`.

# Client servers
- Servers, SSH hosts and stack folders are listed in `docs/deployment.md` ("Current clients"). Use only the access listed there.
- A server may be shared with other apps (for example behind Coolify's Traefik, `compose.coolify.yml`). Never touch other containers, proxies or Coolify, and never reboot or restart Docker.
- Run long commands on a server (builds, `update.sh`) with `nohup` and a log file, and hand back to the developer instead of polling.
- Never print values from `deploy/.env` or `deploy/api.env`; show variable names only. Never ask for passwords or API keys in chat.
- Before anything destructive on the server (deleting volumes, data, containers), back up, explain, and get confirmation.
